    {
      "id": "ev-rules-0002",
      "question": "How does multiball work in Stern\u0027s Godzilla pinball?",
      "expected_sub_agent": "Rules",
      "predicted_sub_agent": "Rules",
      "expected_citation_set": [
        "GweeP-MW95j",
        "GweeP-Ml9pZ"
      ],
      "predicted_citation_set": [
        "GweeP-Ml9pZ"
      ],
      "acceptable_refusal": false,
      "predicted_refusal": false,
      "answer_text": "In **Stern\u0027s Godzilla pinball (2021)** by Keith Elwin, there are several multiball modes, each accessed through specific tasks tied to the playfield features. Here are the main ones:\n\n1. **Godzilla Multiball**:\n   - **How to Start**: Destroy the building by targeting the respective shots. Once the building is destroyed, initiate Godzilla Multiball by shooting under it when lit (green insert indicates readiness).\n   - **During Gameplay**: This is a 3-ball multiball mode where the goal is to hit flashing shots for jackpots and shoot the building for super jackpots. An add-a-ball can be achieved by shooting the green Mechagodzilla targets.\n\n2. **Bridge Attack Multiball**:\n   - **How to Start**: Progress by hitting switch targets to light the captive ball. Hitting the captive ball enough times destroys the bridge, eventually lighting the right ramp to begin this 2-ball multiball.\n   - **During Gameplay**: All lit shots score jackpots. The captive ball is key for 2x jackpots and triggering a timed super jackpot on the right ramp.\n\n3. **Tank Multiball**:\n   - **How to Start**: Complete sequences with green tank shots to light the scoop for Tank Multiball.\n   - **During Gameplay**: Defend against tanks to prevent them from reaching Godzilla. Defeat them successfully to earn jackpots and light the Maser Cannon target for a super jackpot.\n\n4. **Mechagodzilla Multiball**:\n   - **How to Start**: Charge power by hitting the right spinner and the Mechagodzilla shield targets. Once charged, shoot the right spinner again to activate this multiball.\n   - **During Gameplay**: Alternate jackpots between the ramps/building and Mechagodzilla targets. Once all jackpots are scored, build up a super jackpot and complete it at the right spinner.\n\nEach mode includes strategic objectives like building up super jackpots or triggering add-a-ball opportunities for extended play.\n\nFor further details, you can explore a comprehensive game breakdown in the community-written tutorial: Kineticist Godzilla Pinball Tutorial.",
