    {
      "id": "ev-rules-kin-0004",
      "question": "How do I play The Getaway: High Speed II, and how does the supercharger work?",
      "expected_sub_agent": "Rules",
      "predicted_sub_agent": "Rules",
      "expected_citation_set": [
        "Grx8Y-MKNe9"
      ],
      "predicted_citation_set": [
        "Grx8Y-MKNe9"
      ],
      "acceptable_refusal": false,
      "predicted_refusal": false,
      "answer_text": "\u0022The Getaway: High Speed II,\u0022 designed by Steve Ritchie and released by Williams in 1992, is a high-energy pinball machine inspired by police chases. It builds on the original \u0022High Speed\u0022 game by introducing new gameplay mechanics, including the standout feature: the Supercharger. Let\u0027s explore how to play the game and how the Supercharger works.\n\n### Gameplay Overview\nThe core gameplay tasks you with:\n1. **Advancing through gears:** Shoot orbits and other designated shots to collect RPM (Revolutions Per Minute), enabling you to \u0022shift gears\u0022 using the gear shift plunger. Each gear activates high-value modes or awards, such as:\n   - **Video Mode:** Avoid obstacles, shift gears, and collect points while driving.\n   - **Supercharger Mode:** All shots score 5M points, with the Supercharger ramp awarding 5M \u002B 5M per shot.\n   - **Redline Mania:** A wizard-like multiball mode with enhanced scoring opportunities.\n\n2. **Engaging the multiball sequence:** Complete the traffic light targets (green \u2192 yellow \u2192 red) to light locks and start multiball. During multiball:\n   - Shoot 10 Supercharger loops to light jackpots, starting at 25M.\n   - Collect 20 loops to light the Super Jackpot, which escalates to 100M points in Redline Mania.\n\n3. **Scoring Speed Millions:** Repeatedly hit the upper loop to build up rewards.\n\n4. **Using strategic targets:** Completing the 1-2-3 target banks will relight the left outlane\u0027s kickback and increase Supercharger values.\n\n### How the Supercharger Works\nThe Supercharger is a visually stunning and innovative ramp system powered by magnets. Here\u0027s how it functions:\n- When the Supercharger boost is lit (start of the game, multiball modes, or completing 1-2-3 targets), shots to the Supercharger ramp activate the magnets.\n- These magnets accelerate the ball around a circular ramp above the bumpers, creating a dramatic high-speed effect.\n- The system can handle up to three balls simultaneously and counts loops, with each loop contributing to jackpots and super jackpots during multiball.\n\nFor a more detailed breakdown, you can access the full tutorial about gameplay strategies here. Enjoy the chase!",
      "scores": {
        "citation_precision": 1,
        "citation_recall": 1,
        "citation_coverage": 0.14285714285714285,
        "subagent_accuracy": 1,
        "refusal_correctness": 1,
        "answered_all_editions": null,
        "honest_substitution": null,
        "grounding_integrity": 1
      },
